    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1bbe505_141727ee",
        "filename": "ui/status/status.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 127,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-11T22:13:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could see it in this case, but since we\u0027re already locking around calling the outputs in the other cases, I\u0027m not sure it actually improves much. And more advanced terminal status viewers may want to know when the totals have been updated outside of Start/FinishAction. That may largely depends on whether we know about changes to the total due to restat before or after the corresponding FinishAction (in Ninja, it appears to be after).\n\nThis shouldn\u0027t be called very many times during a build -- maybe a dozen times in a normal build, a bit more when we\u0027ve got some restat calls happening. I wouldn\u0027t expect contention, since we usually only have a single build tool active, both Kati and Ninja are implicitly single threaded parsers (I suspect splinter will also be similar for totalActions, since it\u0027ll need to prevent races when counting as well). toolStatus had a lock around calling into here, but I removed that in the next patch.",
      "parentUuid": "00206ab7_165e3f01",
      "revId": "3843f2ed7fba4f6f85f217dbeaa74fdbab1685b7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
