    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a687d8c_5ab194e6",
        "filename": "ui/status/status.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074628
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-11T22:13:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As long as they\u0027re not re-entering the status tool API, this means that the outputs can\u0027t get parallel or out of order requests (and the counts are always correct). They\u0027d nearly all need locks of their own without this, and some way of maintaining order when desired.\n\nThere is the danger of a stuck output halting the entire system, but I don\u0027t know if that can be handled in a particularly better way -- maybe with a per-output buffer. But if we\u0027re blocked writing to the terminal or file system we\u0027ve likely got larger problems. Parallelizing this for loop may be a good first step if this is too slow.",
      "parentUuid": "5ec20d47_bb5ff167",
      "revId": "3843f2ed7fba4f6f85f217dbeaa74fdbab1685b7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
